Dutch National Flag Algorithm (Sort 0s, 1s and 2s)
Definition

The Dutch National Flag Algorithm sorts an array containing only 0s, 1s, and 2s in a single
traversal using three pointers: low, mid, and high.

Key Idea

Maintain four regions:

0 to low-1       → Sorted 0s
low to mid-1     → Sorted 1s
mid to high      → Unsorted elements
high+1 to n-1    → Sorted 2s

Our goal is to shrink the unsorted region (mid to high) until the entire array becomes sorted.

Dutch National Flag Algorithm - Pointwise Notes
 Initialize three pointers:
 low = 0
 mid = 0
 high = n - 1
 Consider the entire array as the unsorted region initially.
 Continue the process while mid <= high.
 If array[mid] == 0:
 Swap array[low] and array[mid].
 Increment low.
 Increment mid.
 This places the 0 in the correct region.
 If array[mid] == 1:
 No swapping is required.
 Increment mid.
 This expands the region containing sorted 1s.
 If array[mid] == 2:
 Swap array[mid] and array[high].
 Decrement high.
 Do not increment mid.
 The element coming from the high position is still unprocessed and must be checked again.
 Repeat until mid > high.
 At this point:
 All 0s are on the left.
 All 1s are in the middle.
 All 2s are on the right.
 The array is completely sorted.

Dutch National Flag Algorithm Dry Run

Array:

[2, 0, 2, 1, 1, 0]

Initial:

low = 0, mid = 0, high = 5

Array:

[2, 0, 2, 1, 1, 0]

Step 1

arr[mid] = 2

Swap arr[mid] and arr[high]

Swap 2 and 0

Array:

[0, 0, 2, 1, 1, 2]

high--

low = 0, mid = 0, high = 4

Step 2

arr[mid] = 0

Swap arr[low] and arr[mid]

Swap 0 and 0

Array:

[0, 0, 2, 1, 1, 2]

low++

mid++

low = 1, mid = 1, high = 4

Step 3

arr[mid] = 0

Swap arr[low] and arr[mid]

Swap 0 and 0

Array:

[0, 0, 2, 1, 1, 2]

low++

mid++

low = 2, mid = 2, high = 4

Step 4

arr[mid] = 2

Swap arr[mid] and arr[high]

Swap 2 and 1

Array:

[0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 2]

high--

low = 2, mid = 2, high = 3

Do not increment mid

Step 5

arr[mid] = 1

No swap

mid++

low = 2, mid = 3, high = 3

Array:

[0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 2]

Step 6

arr[mid] = 1

No swap

mid++

low = 2, mid = 4, high = 3

Array:

[0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 2]

Stop Condition

mid > high

4 > 3

Loop ends.

Final Sorted Array

[0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 2]


Dutch National Flag Algorithm

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)